#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9df7eb-dd1e-53e0-a87d-68b6fd1f480c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481800} {:answer/id #uuid "b3959273-da78-54bd-9652-5e91ff910d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482197} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf2cf7c-d4c9-58ad-ac1c-f6f73d55b4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482226} {:answer/id #uuid "c6299321-746c-562a-a610-1a2b40cd8433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482243} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfaca09-e572-55e6-9c7f-bc94a914bffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcf2cf7c-d4c9-58ad-ac1c-f6f73d55b4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482226} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf4268c8-502e-5529-b80f-13d26b351b38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d66735c3-ba98-5f1c-8e1d-7d80133c59cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-335266" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=9y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0f7256d-2d29-5c85-9d4b-72a842efcbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos(6(t-3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0f7256d-2d29-5c85-9d4b-72a842efcbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos(6(t-3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482307} :answer-field/id #uuid "199ebf62-577b-5ccf-9a87-eb53b5ca9e94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482391} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1cf21ed-005b-59e4-9bd4-7e59ab89d886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(6(t-3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1cf21ed-005b-59e4-9bd4-7e59ab89d886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(6(t-3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482236} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cf580ea-9ff4-59fc-a20f-31f6a8ae4bf6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5cac624-fcaa-5546-985b-94ad2df95205" :question/math-academy-id "q-335436" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(3) \\\\ y(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "% Explanation\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-3)}\\,x(3) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6(t-3))\\, \\\\ \\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(t-3))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59d8cb4f-ee06-5141-9f71-0005f275d41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481984} {:answer/id #uuid "65ee1f50-cf6b-58b8-afd8-663783704016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482010} {:answer/id #uuid "7e285e86-01d4-53c2-bae8-84c094816e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482063} {:answer/id #uuid "d4207d80-a6eb-5165-8ab9-aace8ee2daa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482281} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c4b7e3-8500-59d1-966d-52216ee1c994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c4b7e3-8500-59d1-966d-52216ee1c994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482291} :answer-field/id #uuid "283ab639-7505-5578-b135-707cc7103815" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b9edfd9-1c2b-58af-aab6-8f8f25829073" :question/math-academy-id "q-335447" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(3) \\\\ y(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-3)}\\,x(3) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09fc895b-be35-574c-a0f1-d2e9dbdc5824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481790} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed34351-e7a9-51f4-906b-adec1b5a834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481812} {:answer/id #uuid "96028a64-5f62-51b8-b0ec-6376058e920e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482128} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b37ee0-60b6-54bb-88d3-5a9b8ced5669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09fc895b-be35-574c-a0f1-d2